 "title": "Scalars and vectors",
 "audience": "learner",
 "keyIdea": "A scalar has only a size; a vector has a size and a direction.",
 "explain": {
  "kid": [
   "Some amounts just have a size, like 5 kg or 20 seconds. These are scalars.",
   "Others need a direction too, like 5 m north or a push to the left. These are vectors. We draw them as arrows."
  ],
  "adult": [
   "Scalars: distance, speed, mass, time, energy, temperature. Vectors: displacement, velocity, force, acceleration, momentum.",
   "A vector arrow's length shows its size and its direction shows the way. Run one lap of a 400 m track: the distance is 400 m, but the displacement is 0, because you end at the start."
  ]
 },
